course: dictionary
lesson: 9209
title: Solemn moments
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Solemn is a word for a moment that feels serious and important, when nobody is joking or smiling. «At solemn moments, like a funeral, a minute's silence or the national anthem, you stand still and quiet to show respect.» The clues here are stand still, quiet and respect, so solemn must mean serious and calm.
explain: Look at the words around it. At a funeral, people speak in slow, quiet voices. «The vicar speaks in very formal, old words» because a funeral is solemn. Formal means careful and serious, so solemn fits the mood of the whole service.
explain: Solemn can also describe a promise. A solemn promise is a very serious, sincere promise, one you truly mean. Try swapping in your meaning: «a serious promise» still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
fact: Solemn is an adjective: solemn, more solemn.
fact: «Solemn» means very serious and not happy or joking.
fact: «A solemn promise» is a very serious, sincere promise.
fact: Solemn moments often happen at funerals, at ceremonies, and when people remember those who have died.
fact: «Breathed his last» means died; it is an old-fashioned and solemn way to say it.
exercise: «The room went quiet, and the old man wore a solemn face.» What does solemn mean here? | Very tired and sleepy | *Very serious, not smiling or joking | Very happy and full of jokes | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «She made a solemn promise to keep the secret.» What kind of promise is it? | A short promise, said quickly | *A very serious, sincere promise | A silly promise that is easy to break | A promise made at a party
exercise: «At solemn moments, like a funeral, you stand still and quiet.» Which moment is solemn? | *A funeral | A birthday party | A football match | A picnic in the park
test: Ravi says solemn means funny. Why is he wrong? | Solemn means funny and loud | Solemn means cheerful | Solemn means the same as silly | *Solemn means serious and not joking
test: «Breathed his last» means what? | Fell asleep | Ran away | *Died | Got a new job
exam: Read this: «The vicar spoke in slow, old words at the solemn service.» What does solemn suggest about the service? | *It was serious and respectful | It was a noisy party with music | It was short and silly | It was a game for children
